Scoped support packages are `@package.moth` roots in the project source tree. The containing directory supplies the package name.

### A simple support package

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    @entry.moth
    blog/
    ├── @package.moth
    └── helpers/dates.moth
]

`@package.moth` makes `@blog` a scoped support package visible to the entry root and its normal sibling modules.

### Binding from a package

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    @blog post_title
]

`@blog` resolves to the `blog` directory's support root. The package's public surface comes from its `export:` block.

Support packages can hold reusable ordinary `#` constants. They do not need project metadata.

### The project package

`@package.moth` at the project root is the project's external package surface. Internal project modules cannot import it.

### No pages from support roots

A support root publishes an API and never a page. Only `@entry.moth` creates a page, and importing a support package never runs an entry.
